  "rule_description": "Starting in JDK 9 the Unicode Consortium CLDR data is the default locale data provider; in JDK 8 CLDR was bundled but not enabled. Code that uses locale-sensitive services such as date, time and number formatting can therefore produce different output on JDK 11 than on JDK 8. JADE formats message timestamps through DateFormat.getDateTimeInstance(style, style), which resolves its pattern from the default locale provider, so sniffer and DummyAgent timestamps change shape between JDK 8 and JDK 11. Oracle documents two remedies: set java.locale.providers=COMPAT,CLDR, or stop relying on the provider by stating the pattern explicitly.",
  "rule_id": "CLDR_LOCALE_DATA_DEFAULT",
  "rule_name": "CLDR locale data is the default provider from JDK 9 on",
  "run_id": "jade-8-to-11-v2",
  "sample_size": 5,
